Syntax: transmute <item> <material>

Transmute changes what a thing is made of.  It is what opens the tier ladder
above soft stock, and it is the only bridge between the smith's materials and
the tailor's.

An opal is the price, crushed at the start and gone whether the working takes
or not.  Its carats are what make a hard change possible: every one of them
buys ten off the difficulty.

Distance is what costs.  The materials run metal, crystal, rock, dead,
generic, organic, hide, wood, magical, spiritual, and every family crossed is
ten more against you, plus whatever the target is worth on its own.  Working
inside one family gives back half of what you started with, so mithril into
starmetal is a short reach where cloth into starmetal is the length of the
world.

The length of the working is that same distance plus the weight of the
thing.  Nothing changes until the end: every pulse is counted, and the change
takes only if two thirds of them landed.

See also: PLATE, WEAVE, SMELT
